<Base title="Privacy Policy | Trekking Partners Nepal" description="How Trekking Partners Nepal collects, uses and protects your personal information.">
<article class="doc">
<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="updated">Last updated: 16 October 2026</p>

<p>Trekking Partners Nepal ("we", "us") runs trekkingpartnersnepal.com, a website that helps trekkers find partners for treks in Nepal. This policy explains what information we collect, why, and the choices you have.</p>

<h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>From your Google account</strong>, when you sign in: your name, email address and profile photo. We never see your Google password.</li>
  <li><strong>Profile details you add</strong>: display name, birth year (we show your age, never your birth year), nationality, and optionally your gender.</li>
  <li><strong>Content you post</strong>: trek posts (trek, dates, group size, pace and your message) and replies.</li>
  <li><strong>Reports</strong> you send about posts, replies or trekkers: the reason, any details you add, and that you sent it.</li>
  <li><strong>Basic technical data</strong>: Cloudflare Web Analytics records anonymous page-view statistics without cookies or personal identifiers. Our hosting and login providers process IP addresses for security.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. What is public</h2>
<p>To help trekkers decide whom to walk with, anyone visiting the site can see your display name, profile photo, age, gender (if you added it), nationality, the month you joined, and your trek posts.</p>
<p>Replies are visible only to signed-in members who have completed their profile. Anything you write in a reply, including contact details such as WhatsApp or email, can be read by those members, so share contact details with care.</p>
<p>Your email address and birth year are never shown to other users. The site admin can see your email address to handle reports and abuse. When you report something, the person you reported is not told who reported them.</p>

<h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To create and run your account and show your profile, treks and comments.</li>
  <li>To keep the site safe: limiting how often posts and replies can be sent, investigating reports, removing harmful content and suspending accounts that break our <a href="/terms/">terms</a>.</li>
  <li>To contact you about your account if we need to, for example after a report.</li>
  <li>To understand how the site is used so we can improve it.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for advertising.</p>

<h2>4. Services we use</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Supabase</strong>: database and sign-in (servers in Mumbai, India).</li>
  <li><strong>Google</strong>: "Sign in with Google".</li>
  <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: hosting, security and anonymous analytics.</li>
</ul>
<p>These providers process data on our behalf and may store it on servers outside Nepal.</p>

<h2>5. Cookies</h2>
<p>We use only the browser storage needed to keep you signed in (set by Supabase) and to bring you back to the right page after signing in. We do not use advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

<h2>6. How long we keep data</h2>
<p>We keep your account and content while your account is active. Once a trek's dates have passed, the post no longer appears in listings but can still be opened by its link unless you delete it. If you ask us to delete your account, we remove your profile, posts and replies within 30 days, except where we must keep limited records (such as reports or a ban) to deal with abuse or legal obligations.</p>

<h2>7. Your choices and rights</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Edit your profile details, and close, edit or delete your posts and replies at any time from the site.</li>
  <li>Ask us for a copy of your data, or to delete your account, by emailing <a href="mailto:hello@trekkingpartnersnepal.com">hello@trekkingpartnersnepal.com</a>.</li>
  <li>Revoke the site's access to your Google account at any time in your Google Account settings.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Age</h2>
<p>The site is for people aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect data from anyone younger.</p>

<h2>9. Changes</h2>
<p>If we change this policy, we will update the date at the top and, for significant changes, tell signed-in users on the site.</p>

<h2>10. Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:hello@trekkingpartnersnepal.com">hello@trekkingpartnersnepal.com</a>.</p>
</article>
